      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:15/seg:0",
      "source": "Process context, longer critical sections",
      "source_hash": 7116368508793775955,
      "context_hash": 15883567199684436660,
      "translation": "프로세스 컨텍스트, 긴 임계 구역",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "critical sections": "임계 구역",
        "process": "프로세스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207587Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "rwlock_t: the spinning variant",
      "source_hash": 14567527677903312492,
      "context_hash": 9611631770742814196,
      "translation": "rwlock_t: 스핀 방식 변형",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207587Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "`rwlock_t` is a reader-writer spinlock.",
      "source_hash": 10573021771780524383,
      "context_hash": 8088351091635096107,
      "translation": "`rwlock_t`는 읽기-쓰기 스핀락입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "spinlock": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207587Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "Readers and writers both spin rather than sleep.",
      "source_hash": 6915966774282862316,
      "context_hash": 14057153760440187515,
      "translation": "reader와 writer 모두 슬립하지 않고 스핀합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207587Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "On PREEMPT_RT kernels, `rwlock_t` is implemented with `rwbase_rt` (sleeping), just like `spinlock_t` maps to `rt_mutex`.",
      "source_hash": 6795570266297210154,
      "context_hash": 15640313440275313138,
      "translation": "PREEMPT_RT 커널에서는 `spinlock_t`가 `rt_mutex`에 대응되는 것과 마찬가지로, `rwlock_t`는 `rwbase_rt`(슬립 방식)로 구현됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernels": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207587Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "rw_semaphore: the sleeping variant",
      "source_hash": 10022152786363451339,
      "context_hash": 16342658602687522658,
      "translation": "rw_semaphore: 슬립 방식 변형",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207587Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "`rw_semaphore` is the sleeping counterpart to `rwlock_t`.",
      "source_hash": 15361853513737912210,
      "context_hash": 631063817592204202,
      "translation": "`rw_semaphore`는 `rwlock_t`에 대응하는 슬립 방식 프리미티브입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207587Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "Contended waiters go to sleep rather than spinning (after a brief optimistic spin phase, like mutex).",
      "source_hash": 8636989342723309393,
      "context_hash": 9884285731567087312,
      "translation": "경합 중인 대기자는 스핀하지 않고 슬립합니다(뮤텍스와 마찬가지로 짧은 낙관적 스핀 단계를 거친 뒤입니다).",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "mutex": "뮤텍스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207588Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "The `count` field encodes both the lock state and the reader count.",
      "source_hash": 4503999582980215565,
      "context_hash": 4142216950723974279,
      "translation": "`count` 필드는 락 상태와 reader 수를 함께 인코딩합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207588Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:3/seg:1",
      "source": "The lower bits are flags; the reader count is stored in the upper bits, shifted by `RWSEM_READER_SHIFT` (8):",
      "source_hash": 17198739677769952373,
      "context_hash": 12271007991561048751,
      "translation": "하위 비트는 플래그이며, reader 수는 `RWSEM_READER_SHIFT`(8)만큼 시프트되어 상위 비트에 저장됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "bits": "비트"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207588Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "API",
      "source_hash": 17306549135961116108,
      "context_hash": 18308623999047704784,
      "translation": "API",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "API": "API"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207588Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:7/seg:0",
      "source": "downgrade_write",
      "source_hash": 2284285237206504285,
      "context_hash": 16389868461079823628,
      "translation": "downgrade_write",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207588Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:8/seg:0",
      "source": "`downgrade_write()` atomically converts a write lock to a read lock.",
      "source_hash": 6931543348516095308,
      "context_hash": 14302051334291582767,
      "translation": "`downgrade_write()`는 쓰기 락을 원자적으로 읽기 락으로 전환합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207588Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:8/seg:1",
      "source": "It's used when a writer has finished the write phase and wants to continue reading, while allowing other readers in:",
      "source_hash": 2315686884629820783,
      "context_hash": 1874313953390789338,
      "translation": "이 함수는 writer가 쓰기 단계를 마친 뒤 다른 reader의 진입을 허용하면서 계속 읽기를 수행하려 할 때 사용합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:59.207588Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Writer starvation",
      "source_hash": 11038618010796866132,
      "context_hash": 15694395444099565466,
      "translation": "writer 기아(starvation)",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:49:07.160378Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "A critical problem with naïve reader-writer locks: if readers arrive continuously, a writer may never get the lock.",
      "source_hash": 10144914853592701924,
      "context_hash": 11948758817325993027,
      "translation": "단순한 reader-writer 락의 심각한 문제는, reader가 계속해서 도착하면 writer가 영영 락을 얻지 못할 수도 있다는 점입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:49:07.160379Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "Linux's rwsem prevents this by queuing writers — once a writer is waiting, new readers are also queued (they don't jump ahead of the waiting writer).",
      "source_hash": 13762976776891599723,
      "context_hash": 9578993235954575858,
      "translation": "Linux의 rwsem은 writer를 큐에 넣어 이를 방지합니다. writer가 대기하고 있으면 새 reader도 큐에 들어가며, 대기 중인 writer를 앞질러 가지 않습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "Linux's": "Linux"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:49:07.160379Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "When to use rwlock vs rwsem vs plain mutex/spinlock",
      "source_hash": 1176381599533465371,
      "context_hash": 1482309494910057506,
      "translation": "rwlock, rwsem, 일반 뮤텍스/스핀락 중 무엇을 쓸지",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "mutex": "뮤텍스",
        "spinlock": "스핀락"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:49:07.160380Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Real-world usage: mmap_lock",
      "source_hash": 2554024772072722587,
      "context_hash": 3646031484123716585,
      "translation": "실제 사용 사례: mmap_lock",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:49:07.160381Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "The VMA list in each process is protected by `mm->mmap_lock` (an `rw_semaphore`):",
      "source_hash": 13660334752932848878,
      "context_hash": 852969072531779565,
      "translation": "각 프로세스의 VMA 리스트는 `mm->mmap_lock`(`rw_semaphore`)으로 보호됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "VMA": "VMA",
        "process": "프로세스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:49:07.160381Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "This allows multiple threads in the same process to take page faults concurrently, while mmap/munmap operations are serialized.",
      "source_hash": 4277215710063670350,
      "context_hash": 10045289014276318074,
      "translation": "이 덕분에 같은 프로세스의 여러 스레드가 동시에 페이지 폴트를 처리할 수 있으며, mmap/munmap 연산은 직렬화됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "page faults": "페이지 폴트",
        "process": "프로세스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T21:49:07.160381Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
